! Bookmarks

A bookmark bar for TiddlyWiki, in the shape of a browser's: a thin strip of
favicon-and-name links, with folders that drop open underneath them.

!! Open it
Open the ''Bookmarks'' tiddler (type it in the search box and click it). It
is designed to sit at the top of your wiki, so add `Bookmarks` to
''$:/DefaultTiddlers'' above whatever else you open there.

To keep it in view above the story river instead, tag
''$:/plugins/claude/bookmarks/bar'' with `$:/tags/AboveStory`.

!! Adding bookmarks
Hover the bar and press `+` on the right. Give it:

* a ''URL or tiddler'' — `example.com`, `https://example.com/path` or the
title of a tiddler in this wiki. A bare domain gains `https://`; anything
that is not a URL is treated as a tiddler title, so the bookmark opens that
tiddler instead of a web page.
* a ''name'' — optional. Left blank, a web link is named after its domain and
a tiddler link after the tiddler.
* a ''folder'' — blank puts it straight on the bar. Any other value makes a
folder, and `Dev/Tools` makes ''Tools'' inside ''Dev''.

There is also a ☆ button in the tiddler toolbar: it bookmarks the tiddler
you are reading, and turns into ★ to take it off the bar again.

!! Folders
A folder on the bar opens a dropdown when you click it. Folders nested
inside it expand in place, so you can keep a deep tree without chasing
submenus sideways. A folder exists only while something is in it — empty it
and it disappears from the bar.

!! Rearranging
Press ☰ on the bar for the ''bookmark manager''. Each row there renames a
bookmark, edits its URL or target, moves it to another folder, or deletes
it, and the ↑ ↓ buttons set the order on the bar. Folder headings have the
same arrows, plus ✎ to rename a folder or re-parent it by typing a new
path — blank empties the folder out onto the bar.

!! Icons
Favicons come from DuckDuckGo's icon service by default, which means the
domains you bookmark are requested from `icons.duckduckgo.com` as the bar
renders. Under ''Settings'' in the manager you can switch to Google's
service, fetch `/favicon.ico` from each site directly, or turn favicons off
entirely — the last option draws a coloured initial instead and asks
nothing of the network. Tiddler bookmarks always use an initial.

!! Settings
The manager's ''Settings'' section also hides the names on the bar (leaving
an icon-only strip, names intact inside folders) and chooses whether web
links open in a new tab.

!! Where the bookmarks live
Each bookmark is a tiddler tagged `$:/bookmarks/item`, with `caption`,
`url` or `target`, `folder` and `order` fields. They are system tiddlers, so
they stay out of your searches and sidebar lists, and they travel with the
wiki rather than with this plugin.
